From 387e26e3b91a98303c48508cb07eb5f97e4a9660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qzshch <qzshch@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:53:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] feat(models): sparse-working-set activations across the
 KV store

An address space may now carry an optional device working set (recorded by
apply_device_placement). Its presence changes the activation contract
instead of the data plane:

- prepare/commit_activation scope missing-replica counting, restore
  verification, and the entitlement floor to the working set: activations
  accept window-sized entitlements below the mapped page count and size
  reserved growth past the restored set; dense address spaces (no set)
  keep the exact previous behavior.
- publish_membership publishes by actual residency, so activations and
  snapshots republish holes for Host-only pages while freshly mapped
  growth pages stay live.
- commit_coverage accepts a Host replica as the committing carrier for
  placement-demoted pages; entitlement() reports working set + growth.
- New public queries (page_in_device_working_set, restore_estimate) and
  working-set-scoped restore loops in materialization, request planning,
  and checkpoint recovery replace their dense full-range enumerations.

test_kv_placement grows a sparse-activation case: window reselection,
deactivation, reactivation with entitlement 2 over 4 mapped pages, and a
republished row mixing physical pages with holes.

